**Supplemental control coverage complete.**

This status covers only the requested supplemental controls. It does not certify asymptotic convergence or completion of the eight-ratio onset study.

The duration study uses eta=0.95, degree 43, nr/N=12/132, seed=1e-6, CFL=0.8, diffusion step scale 8, float64, and the z orientation. The same-degree spectral reference is Ra=701.609352. Matched completed runs: original duration 0.2, 3/3; long duration 0.6, 3/3.

Every long-run window uses the same matched triplet. The first three windows are compared with independently fitted original 0.2 runs from the sample root. Differences below are long minus original.

The original short run clips its final timestep to diffusive time 0.2 and writes that endpoint; the long run normally steps past 0.2 without clipping there. The 0.15--0.2 fits therefore need not use the same sample times or sample count. Even samples of an identical underlying trajectory can yield different fitted rates when growth varies within the window. A repeated-window difference can thus reflect endpoint sampling as well as changes in the numerical trajectory; it alone does not establish a physical growth-rate change. The fits use each run's original samples without resampling. Sample counts, sampled intervals, and source provenance are retained in JSON.

